    "body": "Good catch! Yes, when w3c/long-animation-frames#39 fixed `start recording task time if needed` to unwrap `relevant settings object`'s `global object` (`Window`) → `associated Document`, the matching end step in `fire an event` from #1462 was missed.\n\nRather than having `fire an event` unwrap `Window` / `associated Document` and pass `unsafe shared current time` to `record task end time` directly, it's cleaner to keep that in Long Animation Frames by having `start recording task time if needed` return null or cleanup steps (closing over the root `Document` and `unsafe shared current time`), e.g.:\n\n```html\n <li><p>Let <var>endTaskTime</var> be the result of calling\n <a>start recording task time if needed</a> given <var>target</var>'s\n <a>relevant settings object</a>.\n...\n <li><p>If <var>endTaskTime</var> is not null, then run <var>endTaskTime</var>.\n```\n\nThis also avoids a subtle edge case where `target`'s `<iframe>` is detached during `dispatch` (which would otherwise change `nearest same-origin root` before `record task end time` runs).\n\nI've opened w3c/long-animation-frames#50 to update `start recording task time if needed` accordingly; once that lands, we can update this PR to call `endTaskTime` directly.\n",
